From: Jeroen de Vries <j.devries@corp-europe.example>
Sent: Tuesday, 13 October 2026 14:20
To: Hanna Schmidt
Subject: RE: Venlo EWM cut-over date options

January is the problem. The December peak runs into mid-January because of re=
turns and the Q1 promo shipments. Last year we averaged about 2,400 outbound =
deliveries per day in the first three weeks of January, against roughly 1,600=
 per day in February.

Also, our temp staff contracts end on 31 Jan, so a go-live on 30 Jan would pu=
t the new system on the floor exactly when we lose people. 16 Jan is out for =
me, because the training would have to happen in December, the busiest weeks.

So 13 Feb is my preference, but please show me what it does to the training s=
lots.

Kind regards,
